    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "If you've been searching for a home that offers complete privacy, spectacular scenery and modern family living, then this exceptional property at Ballyguiry Upper is sure to impress.\r\nApproached via an impressive 620-foot winding gravel driveway, the house is set well back from the public road, providing a wonderful sense of seclusion while enjoying truly breathtaking panoramic views across the Comeragh and Knockmealdown Mountains, rolling valleys and the surrounding countryside. This is a setting that is becoming increasingly difficult to find, with properties of this nature rarely coming to the market in the South East.\r\nExtending to approximately 1,350 sq. ft., the home has been lovingly maintained and significantly upgraded by its current owners. The heart of the home is undoubtedly the stunning bespoke kitchen, which has been completely renovated within the last 12 months to an exceptional standard. Beautifully designed with both style and functionality in mind, it features premium fitted cabinetry, luxurious stone worktops and matching splashback, a large feature island with additional storage, a Belfast sink and a full range of new high-quality integrated appliances. Every fixture and fitting has been carefully selected to create a timeless contemporary finish. Flooded with natural light and enjoying views over the surrounding gardens, this is an outstanding space for everyday family life and entertaining alike.\r\nThe welcoming living room is positioned to the front of the property and features a fitted solid fuel stove, creating a cosy and inviting atmosphere. There are four generously proportioned bedrooms, including a spacious master bedroom with ensuite, together with a beautifully finished family bathroom. Both bathrooms have been completely refurbished within the past 12 months to a very high standard.\r\nThe property has benefited from extensive improvements in recent years, including a new high-efficiency oil burner, new composite front and patio doors, upgraded cavity wall and attic insulation, partial attic flooring with electricity and Stira access, ensuring the home is both comfortable and energy efficient.\r\nOutside, the mature 1.25-acre site offers exceptional privacy with ample space for children to play, gardening enthusiasts or those simply wishing to enjoy the peaceful surroundings. Despite its tranquil rural setting, the property is just 10 minutes from Dungarvan Town Centre, with local schools, sports clubs and everyday amenities all within easy reach. The scenic drive to town offers beautiful sea views, adding to the appeal of this superb location.\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a beautifully presented family home combining privacy, spectacular mountain views, modern upgrades and an idyllic countryside setting. Early viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate everything this exceptional home has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall\r\nLiving room\r\nKitchen/dining room\r\nUtility Area\r\nBathroom\r\nBedroom one ensuite\r\nBedroom 2\r\nBedroom 3\r\nBedroom 4"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Detached four-bedroom family home \r\nApprox. 1,350 sq. ft. \r\nMature 1.25-acre site \r\nExceptional panoramic views of the Comeragh & Knockmealdown Mountains \r\nPrivate setting with a 620-foot winding gravel driveway \r\nBeautiful bespoke kitchen completely renovated within the last 12 months \r\nPremium fitted kitchen with stone worktops, matching splashback and feature island \r\nNew high-quality integrated appliances \r\nBelfast sink \r\nTwo luxury bathrooms completely refurbished within the last 12 months \r\nBER: C3 \r\nNew high-efficiency oil burner (September 2024) \r\nNew composite front door (December 2024) \r\nNew composite patio doors (February 2025) \r\nNew composite rear door on order \r\nCavity wall insulation and additional attic insulation completed (January 2023) \r\nStira stairs to partially floored attic with electricity \r\nOil-fired central heating \r\nDouble-glazed windows throughout \r\nAlarm \r\nTimber garden shed \r\nWonderful gardens and outdoor space \r\nOnly 10 minutes from Dungarvan Town Centre \r\nA truly peaceful rural setting with nearby schools, sports clubs and local amenities"
